  <text xml:lang="grc">
    <body xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.oidipoys.nauck1889-grc1"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.oidipoys.nauck1889-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:oidipoys"><head xml:lang="grc">ΟΙΔΙΠΟΥΣ</head>
          <note type="introduction" xml:lang="mul">Tetralogiae Oedipodeae fabula secunda, cf. Argum. Aesch. Sept. supra p. 39 allatum. hinc dubitari non potest quin argumentum id fuerit quod in Oedipo Rege tractavit Sophocles. ceterum ut alibi ita hac in fabula perhibetur Aeschylus mystica non nulla evulgasse (vide p. 28) .</note>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="173" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:oidipoys" xml:id="aesch-fr173">
            <lg xml:lang="grc">
              <l n="1" xml:id="nauck-tfg-1-aesch-173-1">ἐπῇμεν τῆς ὁδοῦ τροχήλατον</l>
              <l n="2" xml:id="nauck-tfg-1-aesch-173-2">σχιστῆς κελεύθου τρίοδον, ἔνθα συμβολὰς</l>
              <l n="3" xml:id="nauck-tfg-1-aesch-173-3">τριῶν κελεύθων Ποτνιάδων ἠμείβομεν.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="sourceContext" xml:lang="mul">Schol. Soph. Oed. R. 733 : περὶ Δαυλίδα φησὶ τὴν σχιστὴν ὁδόν ὁ δὲ Αἰσχύλος περὶ Ποτνίας οὕτως ’ἐπῇμεν — ἠμείβομεν’ . Oedipo hos versus adscripsit Valckenaer. v. 1 οὕτως nescimus utrum grammatici sit an Aeschyli. ἐπείημεν ἔπειτ’ ἐπῇμεν . γῆς ὅροις (pro τῆς ὁδοῦ) .</note>
          </div>
        </div></body></text>
